hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"257","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Amr, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of: I went to Aisha and said: Will you not tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy and said: “Did the people pray?” We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God! So he said: “Put water in the basin for me.” She said: So we did so, so he washed himself and then went to take a water bath and fainted. Then he woke up and said: “Did the people pray?” We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God. He said: “Put water in the basin for me.” So we did. She said: So he took a bath, then he went to get the water. He fainted, then he woke up and said: “Did the people pray?” So we said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God. She said: And the people were sitting in the mosque, waiting for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pray. The afterlife dinner. Then he mentioned the hadith in its length"
